\contentsline {table}{\numberline {9.12}{\ignorespaces Comprehensive comparison of all uncertainty quantification methods investigated. The ``Gap to 90\%'' column quantifies the calibration shortfall relative to the nominal 90\% coverage target. Training times reflect wall-clock duration on a single machine with Apple Silicon (M1). Methods are ordered by their underlying approach: single-output BNN variants (rows 1-4), non-Bayesian baselines (rows 5-6), and architectural innovation (row 7).}}{217}{table.caption.1145}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {9.13}{\ignorespaces Phase 1: Feature Ablation Study for BNN Calibration}}{217}{table.caption.1151}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {9.14}{\ignorespaces Bayesian Neural Network Prior Sensitivity Analysis}}{218}{table.caption.1165}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {9.15}{\ignorespaces Phase 3: Uncertainty Quantification Methods Comparison}}{218}{table.caption.1192}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {9.16}{\ignorespaces Bayesian optimization results for single-output BNN hyperparameters (10-trial pilot study). Only 3 of 10 trials completed successfully; the remainder failed due to database query errors when using environment or opponent features. The best configuration (Trial \#0) achieved 34.2\% coverage with Vegas features, 32 hidden units, and $\sigma _{\text {prior}} = 0.548$. This represents only an 8 percentage point improvement over the 26.2\% baseline, leaving a 55.8 percentage point gap to the 90\% target.}}{219}{table.caption.1218}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {9.17}{\ignorespaces Computational cost and return on investment (coverage improvement per compute hour) for each investigation phase. Phase 3 (architectural exploration) provides the highest ROI at 13.2 percentage points per hour, more than 5 times better than feature engineering and 26 times better than prior tuning. This quantifies the efficiency advantage of architectural innovation over hyperparameter engineering.}}{219}{table.caption.1240}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {9.18}{\ignorespaces Decision matrix for practitioners selecting uncertainty quantification methods. No single method dominates across all criteria; choice depends on application priorities. Avoid single-output BNNs for applications requiring calibrated intervals.}}{220}{table.caption.1243}%
